using Browser from std:Browser;
using ui from "./ui.utu";
mod benchmarks {
    fn page() Browser.HTMLElement {
        @wutu/\
        article.page {
            = ui.header("Benchmarks", "The same programs in utu and in nine other languages that compile for the browser: Rust, JavaScript, Dart, Kotlin, MoonBit, AssemblyScript, Go, Swift, and Haskell, each timed in V8, SpiderMonkey, and JavaScriptCore.");
            p {
                "Each program is written once per language, the same way: the same data structures, loops, and order of operations, with only the language's idiom differing. Every port's result is checked against the others in every engine before it is timed.";
            }
            p {
                "Each port runs in each of the three engines' own shells, in a process of its own: V8 15.6.75.16 (d8, as in Chrome, Node, and Deno), SpiderMonkey 154.0 (as in Firefox), and JavaScriptCore built from WebKit in July 2026 (as in Safari and Bun). A time is the median of 20 samples after 5 warmups, in milliseconds.";
            }
            p {
                "A build time is from clean, the median of 3, as each toolchain's command line runs it; utu's is a warm compile in a running process (the whole utu build command takes about 70 ms, most of it starting Node), and Kotlin's has Gradle's daemon already running. A size is everything that must ship to run it: the Wasm and the JavaScript it needs, all minified alike, with gzip per file summed. For utu that JavaScript is the loader utu build writes; for Rust, MoonBit, and AssemblyScript a loader of the same kind; for Dart and Kotlin what their compilers emit; for Go, Swift, and Haskell a WASI shim; JavaScript is just its source.";
            }
            p {
                "utu is built ";
                code {
                    "-O fastUnsafe";
                }
                " and ";
                code {
                    "-O smallUnsafe";
                }
                ", and DeltaBlue also ";
                code {
                    "-O fast";
                }
                " and ";
                code {
                    "-O small";
                }
                " (the default), which keep the checks Wasm does not make itself, such as a Buffer's length. Dart, Kotlin, and MoonBit compile to WasmGC, as utu does. Rust, AssemblyScript, Go, Swift, and Haskell (GHC's WebAssembly backend) compile to linear memory: Rust frees memory itself, while the others carry their own collector or runtime in the module, which is much of their size. Every language keeps its normal checks.";
            }
            p {
                "Run them again with ";
                code {
                    "node scripts/benchmark-programs-d8.mjs --engines=v8,sm,jsc";
                }
                ".";
            }
            h2 {
                "DeltaBlue";
            }
            p {
                "V8's incremental constraint solver: a graph of small objects, planned and re-planned. Chain and projection each solve 1,048 variables 20 times. Rc Rust is a graph of Rc<RefCell<_>> with no unsafe code; unsafe Rust uses an arena and unchecked indexing.";
            }
            table.wide {
                thead {
                    tr {
                        th {
                            "";
                        }
                        th {
                            "chain V8";
                        }
                        th {
                            "chain SM";
                        }
                        th {
                            "chain JSC";
                        }
                        th {
                            "proj. V8";
                        }
                        th {
                            "proj. SM";
                        }
                        th {
                            "proj. JSC";
                        }
                    }
                }
